+% ===================================================================
+\section{What a test of accumulation would need}
+\label{sec:test}
+% ===================================================================
+
+This section is a proposal, not a result: none of it has been run. Each
+element answers one of the confounds documented above.
+
+\begin{enumerate}[nosep]
+    \item \textbf{Fixed neutral assistant turns.} Write the same neutral
+          assistant turns into every arm's history and teacher-force
+          them, instead of sampling the model's own. The stored turns
+          here are planning text that often names the user's tone
+          (Section~\ref{sec:dose}), so sampled turns put the model's own
+          written labels of the tone into the cache, and they differ
+          between arms and between reruns. With fixed turns the arms
+          differ only in their user messages, and the measured turn can
+          hold identical text in every arm, as
+          Section~\ref{sec:dynamics} requires. A tokenizer check should
+          confirm that every fixed turn is encoded in full, with no
+          closing think tag for the chat template to strip.
+    \item \textbf{The recurrent layers, read turn by turn.} Read the
+          state of the 48 linear-attention layers after each turn, as
+          well as the keys of the full-attention layers. That state
+          summarizes the history without per-position keys and is not
+          read here (Section~\ref{sec:dose}, Read layers), so whatever
+          history it carries, this instrument sees only as far as it
+          reaches the keys of four early full-attention layers.
+    \item \textbf{Position-matched or de-rotated keys.} Compare arms
+          only at the same token position, with user messages matched in
+          token length and dose varied at a fixed total length (neutral
+          user turns of the same length standing in for emotional ones),
+          or undo the rotary embedding on the rotated dimensions of each
+          key before projecting. Without one of these, a reading can
+          move with position alone (Section~\ref{sec:dose}; Limitations
+          item~6).
+    \item \textbf{Behavior as ground truth.} Measure whether the model's
+          behavior at the identical measured turn differs across
+          histories, for example in its reply to the same neutral
+          question as judged by readers blind to the arm, before asking
+          whether the geometry tracks it (Limitations item~5).
+\end{enumerate}
+
+The design would also need what the earlier sections already name: at
+least three independent, length-matched scripts per pattern rather than
+more reruns of one (Limitations item~2); turn boundaries found with the
+tokenizer (Section~\ref{sec:dose}); neutral and no-history control arms
+(Limitations item~14); and a text baseline on the same histories
+(Limitations item~9).
+
